  "id": "COMPOUND:30169 - PROTEIN:5798",
  "verbalization": "Leosibirone B, (rel)- is shown to have a direct target relationship with NH-6 through three distinct pathways. The first pathway links Leosibirone B to CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is then identified as a target of a complex molecular entity. The second pathway connects Leosibirone B to Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is also targeted by another molecular entity. In both cases, the target molecules are ultimately linked to NH-6. These findings suggest that Leosibirone B may act through multiple distinct mechanisms to influence NH-6, potentially through different molecular pathways. The evidence supports a possible role for Leosibirone B in modulating the activity of enzymes involved in sialylation and demethylation processes, which are critical for cellular signaling and function. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions involved, and the observed scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship.",
